<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Ravensburg Trading Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1380–<a href="/years/1530">1530</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Große Ravensburger Handelsgesellschaft</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Ravensburg Trading Company was a merchant company formed around 1380 by families of Ravensburg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstanz">Konstanz</a> and other Swabian towns, among them the Humpis. One of the largest trading firms of late medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, it dealt in linen, fustian, saffron and other goods through branches in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. It was dissolved in 1530.</p></div>
